predict-ng 3.0  (May 2026)
==========================
predict-ng is a modernized continuation of John Magliacane's (KD2BD)
classic PREDICT satellite tracking and orbital prediction program.
The binary remains named "predict" for backward compatibility.

New build system
  The old installer.c / build script approach is gone. Build and
  install now follow the standard pattern:

    ./configure [--prefix=DIR] [--enable-vocalizer]
    make
    sudo make install

  No root access needed to run configure. The generated predict.h
  header has been eliminated; version, data directory, and soundcard
  flag are injected as compile-time -D macros.

Vocalizer off by default
  Pass --enable-vocalizer to ./configure to build the voice
  announcement feature (requires /dev/dsp).

East-positive longitude
  Longitude is now stored and entered as degrees East (negative for
  West), matching the standard geographic convention. The -east
  command-line switch is no longer needed for normal use; -west
  is available for West-positive display.

kepupdate rewrite
  kepupdate now fetches TLE data from the current Celestrak GP API
  (https://celestrak.org/) for the amateur, visual, weather, and
  stations groups, merges each into ~/.predict/predict.tle via
  predict -u, and sends SIGHUP to any running predict instance.
  It is installed alongside predict by make install.

  Automate with crontab:
    0 2 * * * kepupdate

SIGHUP live reload
  A running predict instance now reloads predict.tle, predict.qth,
  and predict.db from disk in response to SIGHUP, without restarting.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

PREDICT 2.2.0  (October 2002)
==============================
Major revisions: SGP4/SDP4 orbital models replacing the earlier
simplified model, and a redesigned Single Satellite Tracking Mode
with transponder database support, Doppler-corrected uplink/downlink
frequencies, eclipse depth, and squint angle.

PREDICT 2.1.x series  (2000-2002)
===================================
Highlights: UDP socket server/client architecture, serial port antenna
rotator control (EasyComm 2), solar illumination predictions, lunar
and solar pass predictions, MoonTracker utility, -f and -p command-line
options for scripted position queries, DMS coordinate entry.

PREDICT 2.0.x  (2000)
=======================
Initial public release with socket server code, vocalizer, and the
installer.c-based build system.
